{"id":76294350,"slug":"a-new-standard-of-care-for-severe","title":"A New Standard of Care for Severe Depression?","subtitle":"Remission is the new black.","post_date":"2022-10-03T17:18:43.520Z","audience":"everyone","type":"newsletter","canonical_url":"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/a-new-standard-of-care-for-severe","wordcount":394,"source":"api","fetched_at":"2026-09-13T22:01:23.144Z","body_sha256":"9c80788937b184359db09ee33e60ecd0d7dcf2a0e97c8a97ccbd7e5b33fba030","text_words":392,"complete":true,"body_html":"<p>Current depression treatment guidelines are wrong. By <em>wrong</em>, I mean they don’t do a good job. By <em>don’t do a good job</em> I mean that people suffer for weeks and months longer than they should, and don’t expect to be well at the end of treatment. They expect to have their symptoms managed.</p><p>I’ve got news for the field of psychiatry—even though the <a href=\"https://psychnews.psychiatryonline.org/doi/10.1176/appi.pn.2022.10.8.27\">field of psychiatry doesn’t agree with this approach anymore</a>.  </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Jjmw!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd19471b2-d305-4f60-b1b1-cd498d8b7bf8_1200x1182.jpeg\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Jjmw!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd19471b2-d305-4f60-b1b1-cd498d8b7bf8_1200x1182.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Jjmw!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd19471b2-d305-4f60-b1b1-cd498d8b7bf8_1200x1182.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Jjmw!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd19471b2-d305-4f60-b1b1-cd498d8b7bf8_1200x1182.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Jjmw!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd19471b2-d305-4f60-b1b1-cd498d8b7bf8_1200x1182.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Jjmw!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd19471b2-d305-4f60-b1b1-cd498d8b7bf8_1200x1182.jpeg\" width=\"1200\" height=\"1182\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://bucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/d19471b2-d305-4f60-b1b1-cd498d8b7bf8_1200x1182.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1182,&quot;width&quot;:1200,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:286710,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Jjmw!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd19471b2-d305-4f60-b1b1-cd498d8b7bf8_1200x1182.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Jjmw!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd19471b2-d305-4f60-b1b1-cd498d8b7bf8_1200x1182.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Jjmw!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd19471b2-d305-4f60-b1b1-cd498d8b7bf8_1200x1182.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Jjmw!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd19471b2-d305-4f60-b1b1-cd498d8b7bf8_1200x1182.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>In a sensible world, it would be acknowledged that an approach to massive blood loss that only involved IV fluids is insufficient. If gaping-wound-care never involved stitching up the gaping wound, as a first line approach, it would be a strange world.  You’d probably want to give people with massive blood loss extra blood. And you’d probably want to stitch up the hole from which the blood was exiting.</p><p>Similarly, for the second leading cause of death in the young, you’d want to have the most robust treatments with the least side effects which also had the largest chance of resolving the problem <em>come first</em>.  </p><p>The APA, via Psych News, <a href=\"https://psychnews.psychiatryonline.org/doi/10.1176/appi.pn.2022.10.8.27\">posted an article today</a>, authored by my friend and colleague Rich Bermudez, MD. Here is the data he presented:</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!9EFi!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1e7ac27f-1580-4f74-8a43-35083a7049e1_929x265.jpeg\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!9EFi!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1e7ac27f-1580-4f74-8a43-35083a7049e1_929x265.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!9EFi!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1e7ac27f-1580-4f74-8a43-35083a7049e1_929x265.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!9EFi!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1e7ac27f-1580-4f74-8a43-35083a7049e1_929x265.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!9EFi!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1e7ac27f-1580-4f74-8a43-35083a7049e1_929x265.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!9EFi!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1e7ac27f-1580-4f74-8a43-35083a7049e1_929x265.jpeg\" width=\"929\" height=\"265\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://bucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/1e7ac27f-1580-4f74-8a43-35083a7049e1_929x265.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:265,&quot;width&quot;:929,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:147904,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!9EFi!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1e7ac27f-1580-4f74-8a43-35083a7049e1_929x265.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!9EFi!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1e7ac27f-1580-4f74-8a43-35083a7049e1_929x265.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!9EFi!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1e7ac27f-1580-4f74-8a43-35083a7049e1_929x265.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!9EFi!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1e7ac27f-1580-4f74-8a43-35083a7049e1_929x265.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>Transcranial magnetic stimulation (TMS) has been around since the 1980s, and been an FDA approved treatment since 2008. Now that it’s 2022, we should probably consider using it. If you’re wondering what pharmacotherapy is, it means every medication you’ve ever heard about. Anti-depressants. You know, the kind of things that can be prescribed by any tele-health-only prescriber. </p><p>TMS requires your physical body to be present. Because it stimulates your brain—part of your body—with a magnet. In person.</p><p>If you were suffering from moderate to severe depression, and you were offered a choice of a 36% chance of remission or a 63% chance of remission… which would you take first?</p><p>The current standard of care is to recommend the thing that doesn’t work very well first. This <em>may</em> make sense for mild depression.  </p><p>But if it’s a serious problem, let’s stop the problem in a way that is effective and is most likely to work. The fact that it’s more tolerable is just a bonus.</p><p>Severe depression: we shouldn’t perpetuate its existence by insisting on less effective treatments as the first line.</p><p>—O. Scott Muir, M.D.</p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p><p></p>","text":"Current depression treatment guidelines are wrong. By wrong , I mean they don’t do a good job. By don’t do a good job I mean that people suffer for weeks and months longer than they should, and don’t expect to be well at the end of treatment. They expect to have their symptoms managed.\n\nI’ve got news for the field of psychiatry—even though the field of psychiatry doesn’t agree with this approach anymore .\n\nIn a sensible world, it would be acknowledged that an approach to massive blood loss that only involved IV fluids is insufficient. If gaping-wound-care never involved stitching up the gaping wound, as a first line approach, it would be a strange world. You’d probably want to give people with massive blood loss extra blood. And you’d probably want to stitch up the hole from which the blood was exiting.\n\nSimilarly, for the second leading cause of death in the young, you’d want to have the most robust treatments with the least side effects which also had the largest chance of resolving the problem come first .\n\nThe APA, via Psych News, posted an article today , authored by my friend and colleague Rich Bermudez, MD. Here is the data he presented:\n\nTranscranial magnetic stimulation (TMS) has been around since the 1980s, and been an FDA approved treatment since 2008. Now that it’s 2022, we should probably consider using it. If you’re wondering what pharmacotherapy is, it means every medication you’ve ever heard about. Anti-depressants. You know, the kind of things that can be prescribed by any tele-health-only prescriber.\n\nTMS requires your physical body to be present. Because it stimulates your brain—part of your body—with a magnet. In person.\n\nIf you were suffering from moderate to severe depression, and you were offered a choice of a 36% chance of remission or a 63% chance of remission… which would you take first?\n\nThe current standard of care is to recommend the thing that doesn’t work very well first. This may make sense for mild depression.\n\nBut if it’s a serious problem, let’s stop the problem in a way that is effective and is most likely to work. The fact that it’s more tolerable is just a bonus.\n\nSevere depression: we shouldn’t perpetuate its existence by insisting on less effective treatments as the first line.\n\n—O. Scott Muir, M.D.\n\nSubscribe now"}